      "writtenOn": "2024-03-15T13:03:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "style question, do we really want to have the #define around the entire class and functions calls? Alternatively, we just put the #defines inside each function. The argument for doing the later is that this way we don\u0027t have two copies of the same function signature. If we ever decide to update them, I can easily see this be a pain that we always miss updating one since locally it won\u0027t build one version. Then we get yelled out by the bots.\n\nAnyways curious what you guys think about each approach. I think I lean towards having it in each function, but can easily be convinced otherwise.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 35,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 35,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "1a10f72b80a30b10f252377a7cd3a18542b3116e",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
