      "writtenOn": "2024-03-15T18:09:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I also prefer defining two separate classes to make it clearer. However, unfortunately, in this case, neither wgpu::Future nor WaitAny is available in wasm. So we cannot avoid #ifdef.\n\nOn the other hand, I personally feel #ifdef inside functions less readable than #ifdef the entire class. It\u0027s true that we might miss updating functions\u0027 signatures in one config due to it not being compiled locally. But that\u0027s also applied to the code inside the #ifdef, we could miss the compiling errors inside it too. So this kind of problem is unavoidable with #ifdef.",
      "parentUuid": "268a7898_312652a2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 35,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 35,
        "endChar": 27
      },
